From: Project Luma <maintainers@projectluma.org>
Subject: [PATCH] nautilus: mark the root toolbar as window material

Filer's outer AdwToolbarView owns the application header, but unlike native
Luma application windows it was never marked as the window toolbar view.  The
shared Developer Platform therefore could not clear libadwaita's generated
top-bar wrapper for Frost and Glass, leaving an opaque strip above otherwise
translucent content.

Adopt the shared structural role on that root toolbar only.  The nested
sidebar and content toolbar views remain island surfaces and keep their own
material ownership.

---
 src/resources/ui/nautilus-window.blp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/resources/ui/nautilus-window.blp b/src/resources/ui/nautilus-window.blp
--- a/src/resources/ui/nautilus-window.blp
+++ b/src/resources/ui/nautilus-window.blp
@@ -169,6 +169,7 @@ template $NautilusWindow: Adw.ApplicationWindow {
   $NautilusShortcutManager {
     child: Adw.ToastOverlay toast_overlay {
       child: Adw.ToolbarView {
+        styles ["luma-window-toolbar-view"]
         [top]
         Adw.HeaderBar {
           show-start-title-buttons: false;
-- 
